{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3cb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07db8-a28a-7e80-8be1-e3a988123386"},"sequence":64,"recorded_at":1780531400000123,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4385e4d6-e071-42f2-a438-a44213370546","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"4385e4d6-e071-42f2-a438-a44213370546","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4385e4d6-e071-42f2-a438-a44213370546"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"426be621-1c43-4946-ab46-d10f7813b166"},"task_id":"426be621-1c43-4946-ab46-d10f7813b166","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"426be621-1c43-4946-ab46-d10f7813b166","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-1r9wrr/TASK-260830-1r9wrr_review-verdict-rev1.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-1r9wrr — review verdict, CR-TASK-260830-1r9wrr-1 rev1\n2|\n3|**Verdict: changes requested → `to-dev`.**\n4|**repeat-of: none** (first revision of this leaf).\n5|\n6|Candidate re-derived at review time: detached-index `git read-tree HEAD` + add of\n7|the 16 CR paths → tree `95b2f9e58f00ee9aea5aba32c548bcc1e44e5a34`, equal to the\n8|recorded candidate tree; `git ls-tree -r` confirms all 14 new `internal/sessstate`\n9|files are in that tree (not an index that silently dropped the untracked package).\n10|Working tree restored to that exact OID after every plant and mutant below —\n11|re-verified as the last action of this review.\n12|\n13|The production code is largely sound and the division of authority is real. Four\n14|findings block acceptance: two are derivation defects inside the AC's own scope\n15|that no test pins, one is a census whose denominator is a single function name\n16|(a behaviourally wrong plant walks through all three censuses and the whole\n17|suite), and one is a wrong published number in the shipped `README.md`.\n18|\n19|---\n20|\n21|## What I drove myself (exit codes observed in this run)\n22|\n23|| Gate | Command | Exit |\n24|| --- | --- | --- |\n25|| package baseline | `go test ./internal/sessstate/ -count=1` | 0 |\n26|| repo-wide suite | `go test ./... -count=1` | 0 (25 packages ok, 0 FAIL) |\n27|| build | `go build ./...` | 0 |\n28|| vet | `go vet ./internal/sessstate/` | 0 |\n29|| windows | `GOOS=windows go build ./...`, `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` | 0, 0 |\n30|| format | `gofmt -l internal/sessstate/` | no output |\n31|| tracecheck | `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` | 0 |\n32|| coverage | `go test ./internal/sessstate/ -cover` | 0 — 91.7% of statements (claim matches) |\n33|| race | `go test -race ./internal/sessstate/ ./internal/sessrepo/ -count=1` | 0 |\n34|| reviewer battery | 13 mutants, harness `.temp/TASK-260830-1r9wrr/review/rmutate.sh` | 10 killed, **3 survived** |\n35|| census plants | 5 plants, harness `.temp/TASK-260830-1r9wrr/review/plants.sh` | 4 killed, **1 survived** |\n36|| behavioural probes | 7 probes through `Reduce`/`Project` | 3 confirmed defects, 3 refuted, 1 bound |\n37|\n38|**Not re-run by me, accepted as the producer reported it:** the 4-group `-race`\n39|split over all 25 packages (I ran 2 of them), and the six pinned `cigate`\n40|contract selections. The attached rev1 validation log is truncated (65 536 bytes,\n41|~5.2 MB dropped) and was not used as evidence for anything above.\n42|\n43|---\n44|\n45|## F1 — `resolveWinner`: a duplicated off-chain union lease erases the\n46|## `union_supersedes_chain` conflict and the `divergent_history` warning\n47|\n48|`internal/sessstate/sessstate.go`, `resolveWinner`, the `case 0:` arm:\n49|\n50|```go\n51|case 0:\n52|    if _, ok := onChain[lease.LeaseID]; !ok {\n53|        offChainWinner = false\n54|    }\n55|```\n56|\n57|`Compare(lease, winner) == 0` with `lease.LeaseID` **not** on the chain is only\n58|reachable *after* `winner` has already been moved to an off-chain union lease by\n59|an earlier iteration. So the arm's only reachable effect is to clear the flag\n60|that a previous iteration correctly set.\n61|\n62|Driven through the production `Reduce` entry (chain `session.created` +\n63|`provider.launched`, head lease `(1, aaaaaaaa-…)`):\n64|\n65|```\n66|Union: [(3, cccccccc-…)]              -> winner (3, cccccccc-…), conflicts=1\n67|                                          kind=union_supersedes_chain rule=authoritative-state-unchanged\n68|Union: [(3, cccccccc-…), (3, cccccccc-…)]\n69|                                      -> winner (3, cccccccc-…), conflicts=0, warnings=[]\n70|```\n71|\n72|Same winner, conflict and warning gone. AC row 3 requires a conflict where both\n73|sides are individually valid to be \"refused or resolved by a named rule\"; here it\n74|is silently dropped, and the `divergent_history` warning `emitWarnings` derives\n75|from it disappears with it.\n76|\n77|**Mutant R2** — delete the arm body (`case 0: _ = onChain`) — **SURVIVED** both\n78|gates (`behavioral=PASS full=PASS`). The branch has zero test coverage; its only\n79|observable behaviour is the defect.\n80|\n81|## F2 — `applyLocalLease`: a local lease that WON the tuple rule is reported `stale`\n82|\n83|```go\n84|if Compare(local, fold.projection.Winner) == 0 {\n85|    return\n86|}\n87|```\n88|\n89|The rule is documented three times as *lost*: the function comment (\"a local\n90|lease that lost the tuple rule stales the projection\"), `Projector.Local`'s field\n91|doc, and `README.md` (\"a local lease that lost the tuple rule stales the local\n92|projection the same way\"). It is implemented as *not equal*.\n93|\n94|Driven through `Reduce` (chain head `(1, aaaaaaaa-…)`, `Local: (9, cccccccc-…)`):\n95|\n96|```\n97|state=\"stale\"  winner={Epoch:1 LeaseID:aaaaaaaa-…}  warnings=[stale_process]\n98|```\n99|\n100|The host holding the strictly greater lease is reported stale with a\n101|`stale_process` warning — a wrong `SessionState` value under AC row 1 and a wrong\n102|winner story under AC row 2.\n103|\n104|**Mutant R1** — the candidate fix `Compare(...) >= 0` — **SURVIVED** both gates.\n105|The suite does not distinguish the two, so nothing pins the current behaviour\n106|either way. (Applying the candidate fix and seeing whether the suite notices is\n107|the check that separates \"intended\" from \"unmeasured\": it is unmeasured.)\n108|\n109|**F1 and F2 together refute the outcome's claim** \"26 applied, 26 killed, 0\n110|survivors. No surviving mutant exists, so no survival bound is owed.\" Both are\n111|narrowing mutants on production gates inside AC rows 2 and 3; the battery's\n112|12 narrowing rows touch `Compare`, the gap arm, the transition table, the retry\n113|gates, the provider arms, the lease-linkage arms and the parked branch, but not\n114|one of them reaches `resolveWinner`'s off-chain bookkeeping or `applyLocalLease`.\n115|The denominator excluded the half of the winner derivation that carries the\n116|defects.\n117|\n118|## F3 — the event census's denominator is one function name; a second handling\n119|## site with a wrong effect walks through everything\n120|\n121|`deriveHandledEventTypes` (census_state_test.go) inspects only\n122|`FuncDecl.Name == \"effect\"`. Plant **PA**: a new production file\n123|`internal/sessstate/zz_plant.go` declaring\n124|\n125|```go\n126|func (fold *chainFold) effectExtra(event Event, what string) error {\n127|    switch event.Type {\n128|    case \"session.reaped\":\n129|        return fold.step(StateIdle, what)\n130|    }\n131|    return nil\n132|}\n133|```\n134|\n135|wired into the production switch by the one-line, line-count-preserving edit\n136|`default: return nil` → `default: return fold.effectExtra(event, name)`.\n137|\n138|Result: **SURVIVED** — `behavioral=PASS full=PASS`. An unknown v1 event type now\n139|moves `running → idle`, directly contradicting the Section 5.2 inert rule this\n140|package claims to enforce and its own\n141|`TestReduceTreatsUnknownV1TypeAsInert` (which drives a different spelling,\n142|`session.future_probe`). All three censuses stay green: the refusal census sees\n143|no new `refuse` site, the state census sees no new spelling, and the event census\n144|never looks outside `effect`.\n145|\n146|So \"24 handled types == the pinned v1 registry, both directions\" is a claim about\n147|one function, not about production. Fix by deriving the denominator from every\n148|production event-type dispatch, or by failing closed when a second dispatch site\n149|on `event.Type` exists.\n150|\n151|The other four plants were correctly killed, so the fix is narrow:\n152|\n153|| Plant | Shape | Outcome |\n154|| --- | --- | --- |\n155|| PA | fresh-spelling handler in a new production file, wired into `effect` | **SURVIVED** |\n156|| PB | `var deny = refuse` in a new production file | KILLED (alias audit, `zz_plant.go:3:12`) |\n157|| PC | `var parseDigest = scalar.ParseDigest` (alias-bound owner delegation) | KILLED (alias audit, `zz_plant.go:5:26`) |\n158|| PD | `const StateReaped State = \"reaped\"` in a new production file | KILLED (`TestStateSpaceIsCensused`) |\n159|| PE | direct `refuse(ErrIntegrity, …)` at a new production site | KILLED (`TestRefusalSitesAreCensused`) |\n160|\n161|## F4 — the published refusal-census denominator is wrong in the shipped README\n162|\n163|`README.md:1763-1764` and the outcome both state:\n164|\n165|> the 67-site refusal inventory … (39 in `sessstate.go`, 26 in `decode.go`, 2 in\n166|> `project.go`)\n167|\n168|The roster in `census_state_test.go` has **69** rows — 39 / **28** / 2 — and\n169|`TestRefusalSitesAreCensused` requires derived == roster in *both* directions and\n170|passes, so the derived count is 69 and `decode.go` carries 28 sites, not 26.\n171|This contradicts the outcome's own \"every number below re-derived after the last\n172|artifact\". Re-derive the number in source and correct both `README.md` and the\n173|outcome.\n174|\n175|## F5 — neither harness control exercised either gate (instrument, not production)\n176|\n177|```\n178|X1: NOT_APPLIED (pattern count=0)\n179|X2: COMPILE_FAIL\n180|```\n181|\n182|X1 is an intentionally absent pattern and X2 is a syntax break, so both exit\n183|before `go test` runs. Nothing in the producer's evidence shows the harness can\n184|report **SURVIVED** — the outcome that every one of the 26 KILLED rows is\n185|measured against — and `README.md` advertises them as \"plus NOT_APPLIED and\n186|COMPILE_FAIL controls\" without that distinction.\n187|\n188|I supplied the missing control: **R0**, behaviour-neutral and line-count\n189|preserving (`tailEventID` returning `\"\" + fold.tailID`) → **SURVIVED**. With\n190|R3–R10 (8 compiling known-bad mutants, all `behavioral=FAIL`) the instrument is\n191|sound in both directions — but that is my evidence, not the delivered evidence.\n192|Ship a real pair: one neutral mutant that must survive, one known-bad that must\n193|redden, both reaching the gates.\n194|\n195|## F6 (minor) — `scalar.ParseUUIDv7` is an unmeasured audit row and an\n196|## unsupported doc claim\n197|\n198|`doc.go:36-37` and `README.md:1775` name `scalar.ParseUUIDv7` among the watched\n199|owner delegations \"for digest and UUID grammars\". It has **zero** occurrences in\n200|`internal/sessstate` production (`environ.CheckUUIDv7` does that work). The\n201|alias-audit row can never fire, and the documentation states a delegation the\n202|package does not make.\n203|\n204|## F7 (minor) — an empty chain skips union validation entirely\n205|\n206|`Reduce` returns `creating` before `resolveWinner` when `len(input.Events) == 0`,\n207|so `Input.Union` and `Input.Local` are neither validated nor applied:\n208|\n209|```\n210|Union: [{4, \"not-a-uuid\"}, {}]  ->  state=\"creating\"  winner={0 \"\"}  err=<nil>\n211|```\n212|\n213|The same union on a non-empty chain refuses `ErrInvalidEvent` at\n214|`sessstate.go:920` / `:923`. Make it a gate or a stated bound in `doc.go`.\n215|\n216|---\n217|\n218|## Reviewer mutation battery (13 mutants; 10 killed, 3 survived)\n219|\n220|| ID | Mutation | Result |\n221|| --- | --- | --- |\n222|| R0 | neutral: `tailEventID` returns `\"\" + fold.tailID` | **SURVIVED** (negative control, as intended) |\n223|| R0b | `if found.Parked` → `if found == nil \\|\\| found.Parked` | SURVIVED — my error, the arm is unreachable (`found == nil` already returned); a second neutral control, not a positive one |\n224|| R1 | `Compare(local, Winner) == 0` → `>= 0` | **SURVIVED** — F2 |\n225|| R2 | delete the `case 0:` off-chain reset in `resolveWinner` | **SURVIVED** — F1 |\n226|| R3 | `staleSources` admits `stopped` | KILLED — `TestProjectLeavesStoppedPastTakeoverUnstaled` |\n227|| R4 | transition table admits `running → stopped` | KILLED — `TestReduceRefusesUnlistedTransitions/running-to-stopped` |\n228|| R5 | `noteCheckpoint` keeps the oldest instead of the newest | KILLED — `TestProjectDerivesFullLifecycle` |\n229|| R6 | provider version recorded even on record mismatch | KILLED — `TestProviderMismatchKeepsRecordPinned` |\n230|| R7 | local role inverted | KILLED — `TestProjectDerivesFullLifecycle`, `TestProjectIsIdempotentAcrossReads` |\n231|| R8 | `stale_process` warning suppressed | KILLED — `TestProjectDerivesLocalStale` |\n232|| R9 | epoch-gap conflict only past a jump of 3 | KILLED — `TestWinnerResolutionGap` |\n233|| R10 | losing-branch conflict dropped for epoch-1 rivals | KILLED — `TestWinnerResolutionTie`, `…TieOrdersBytewise`, `…PastEpochTie` |\n234|\n235|Every row above compiles and reaches both gates, so the denominator is 13 of 13\n236|applied; killed-over-applied is 10/13, with the three survivors named.\n237|\n238|---\n239|\n240|## Checked and clean (probed, refuted as findings — do not re-litigate)\n241|\n242|- **`task_board.launched.state` and `session.stopped.closure_kind` are not admit\n243|  holes.** Both `else` arms looked ungated on reading, but the canonical owner\n244|  closes them upstream: `core_records.go:859` `enum(\"state\",\"running\",\"idle\")`\n245|  and `core_records.go:742` `requireEnum(…,\"checkpointed\",\"bootstrap_abort\")`.\n246|  Fixtures carrying `\"tombstoned\"` / `\"crashed\"` are rejected by\n247|  `CalculateObjectIdentity` before they can reach `Reduce`. The `doc.go` claim\n248|  that the payload members `Reduce` reads were admitted by the closed shape holds.\n249|- **Multiple predecessors on a non-first event are correct, not a divergence.**\n250|  Section 5.2 declares predecessors as \"a sorted array of one or more digests\"\n251|  and `sessrepo/chain.go:191` applies the identical\n252|  `containsDigest(predecessors, tail)` rule. `Reduce` mirrors its owner exactly.\n253|- **AC row 9 crash points sit inside the window they claim.** All four\n254|  `armCreateStep` tests assert `injector.RemainingArmed()` is empty after the\n255|  faulted `CreateSession`, so the armed point provably fired; the four targets\n256|  are the four `CreateStep` boundaries (`SessionDir`, `Record`, `EventsDir`,\n257|  `Chain`), one per boundary, and each of the first three heals on the identical\n258|  retry.\n259|- **Purity holds one step out from the producer's own vectors.** On a 5-event\n260|  chain with a forced-lease succession, a two-entry union and a local lease: 64\n261|  concurrent `Reduce` calls all `reflect.DeepEqual` to the sequential result;\n262|  `Input` (including `Events` and `Union`) is unmutated by the call; and\n263|  tampering with the returned `Conflicts`/`Warnings` slices does not leak into a\n264|  later call — no aliasing across invocations. `-race` on the package: exit 0.\n265|- **The untouched-package claims hold.** The CR delta is exactly 16 paths\n266|  (`LOGBOOK.md`, `README.md`, 14 files under `internal/sessstate/`); no\n267|  `internal/sessrepo` or `internal/provhost` file is touched, and no package in\n268|  the repository imports `internal/sessstate` yet.\n269|- **AC-row coverage: 10 of 10 rows name a driving test that exists and is green**,\n270|  including `TestNoProductionPathAttestsProviderIdentityBinding`\n271|  (`internal/provhost/identity_test.go:95`) for row 10 and `tracecheck` exit 0.\n272|  The ratio is honest; F1/F2 are holes *inside* rows 2 and 3, not missing rows.\n273|\n274|---\n275|\n276|## What to do next\n277|\n278|1. Fix `resolveWinner`'s `case 0:` arm (F1) and `applyLocalLease`'s comparison\n279|   (F2), and pin each with a test that fails on the current code — a duplicated\n280|   off-chain union entry, and a local lease strictly greater than the winner.\n281|   Verify one step away from the finding vector, not only at it.\n282|2. Widen the event census denominator so a second production dispatch on\n283|   `event.Type` cannot be invisible (F3), and keep PA as a control plant.\n284|3. Re-derive and correct the 67/26 numbers in `README.md` and the outcome (F4).\n285|4. Add a real pair of harness controls that reach the gates — one neutral mutant\n286|   that must survive, one known-bad that must redden (F5).\n287|5. Fix or drop the `scalar.ParseUUIDv7` claim (F6) and gate-or-bound the\n288|   empty-chain union path (F7).\n289|6. Extend the battery's narrowing rows to the union/local-lease derivation; the\n290|   current denominator excludes it."}}}
