{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3d3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07db8-a28a-7e80-8be1-e3a988123386"},"sequence":68,"recorded_at":1780531400000131,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4385e4d6-e071-42f2-a438-a44213370546","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"4385e4d6-e071-42f2-a438-a44213370546","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4385e4d6-e071-42f2-a438-a44213370546"},"call_id":"call_01a07db8cc2778229f6330ec13702069","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-1r9wrr/TASK-260830-1r9wrr_review-verdict-rev1.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-1r9wrr — review verdict, CR-TASK-260830-1r9wrr-1 rev1\n2|\n3|**Verdict: changes requested → `to-dev`.**\n4|**repeat-of: none** (first revision of this leaf).\n5|\n6|Candidate re-derived at review time: detached-index `git read-tree HEAD` + add of\n7|the 16 CR paths → tree `95b2f9e58f00ee9aea5aba32c548bcc1e44e5a34`, equal to the\n8|recorded candidate tree; `git ls-tree -r` confirms all 14 new `internal/sessstate`\n9|files are in that tree (not an index that silently dropped the untracked package).\n10|Working tree restored to that exact OID after every plant and mutant below —\n11|re-verified as the last action of this review.\n12|\n13|The production code is largely sound and the division of authority is real. Four\n14|findings block acceptance: two are derivation defects inside the AC's own scope\n15|that no test pins, one is a census whose denominator is a single function name\n16|(a behaviourally wrong plant walks through all three censuses and the whole\n17|suite), and one is a wrong published number in the shipped `README.md`.\n18|\n19|---\n20|\n21|## What I drove myself (exit codes observed in this run)\n22|\n23|| Gate | Command | Exit |\n24|| --- | --- | --- |\n25|| package baseline | `go test ./internal/sessstate/ -count=1` | 0 |\n26|| repo-wide suite | `go test ./... -count=1` | 0 (25 packages ok, 0 FAIL) |\n27|| build | `go build ./...` | 0 |\n28|| vet | `go vet ./internal/sessstate/` | 0 |\n29|| windows | `GOOS=windows go build ./...`, `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` | 0, 0 |\n30|| format | `gofmt -l internal/sessstate/` | no output |\n31|| tracecheck | `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` | 0 |\n32|| coverage | `go test ./internal/sessstate/ -cover` | 0 — 91.7% of statements (claim matches) |\n33|| race | `go test -race ./internal/sessstate/ ./internal/sessrepo/ -count=1` | 0 |\n34|| reviewer battery | 13 mutants, harness `.temp/TASK-260830-1r9wrr/review/rmutate.sh` | 10 killed, **3 survived** |\n35|| census plants | 5 plants, harness `.temp/TASK-260830-1r9wrr/review/plants.sh` | 4 killed, **1 survived** |\n36|| behavioural probes | 7 probes through `Reduce`/`Project` | 3 confirmed defects, 3 refuted, 1 bound |\n37|\n38|**Not re-run by me, accepted as the producer reported it:** the 4-group `-race`\n39|split over all 25 packages (I ran 2 of them), and the six pinned `cigate`\n40|contract selections. The attached rev1 validation log is truncated (65 536 bytes,\n41|~5.2 MB dropped) and was not used as evidence for anything above.\n42|\n43|---\n44|\n45|## F1 — `resolveWinner`: a duplicated off-chain union lease erases the\n46|## `union_supersedes_chain` conflict and the `divergent_history` warning\n47|\n48|`internal/sessstate/sessstate.go`, `resolveWinner`, the `case 0:` arm:\n49|\n50|```go\n51|case 0:\n52|    if _, ok := onChain[lease.LeaseID]; !ok {\n53|        offChainWinner = false\n54|    }\n55|```\n56|\n57|`Compare(lease, winner) == 0` with `lease.LeaseID` **not** on the chain is only\n58|reachable *after* `winner` has already been moved to an off-chain union lease by\n59|an earlier iteration. So the arm's only reachable effect is to clear the flag\n60|that a previous iteration correctly set.\n61|\n62|Driven through the production `Reduce` entry (chain `session.created` +\n63|`provider.launched`, head lease `(1, aaaaaaaa-…)`):\n64|\n65|```\n66|Union: [(3, cccccccc-…)]              -> winner (3, cccccccc-…), conflicts=1\n67|                                          kind=union_supersedes_chain rule=authoritative-state-unchanged\n68|Union: [(3, cccccccc-…), (3, cccccccc-…)]\n69|                                      -> winner (3, cccccccc-…), conflicts=0, warnings=[]\n70|```\n71|\n72|Same winner, conflict and warning gone. AC row 3 requires a conflict where both\n73|sides are individually valid to be \"refused or resolved by a named rule\"; here it\n74|is silently dropped, and the `divergent_history` warning `emitWarnings` derives\n75|from it disappears with it.\n76|\n77|**Mutant R2** — delete the arm body (`case 0: _ = onChain`) — **SURVIVED** both\n78|gates (`behavioral=PASS full=PASS`). The branch has zero test coverage; its only\n79|observable behaviour is the defect.\n80|\n81|## F2 — `applyLocalLease`: a local lease that WON the tuple rule is reported `stale`\n82|\n83|```go\n84|if Compare(local, fold.projection.Winner) == 0 {\n85|    return\n86|}\n87|```\n88|\n89|The rule is documented three times as *lost*: the function comment (\"a local\n90|lease that lost the tuple rule stales the projection\"), `Projector.Local`'s field\n91|doc, and `README.md` (\"a local lease that lost the tuple rule stales the local\n92|projection the same way\"). It is implemented as *not equal*.\n93|\n94|Driven through `Reduce` (chain head `(1, aaaaaaaa-…)`, `Local: (9, cccccccc-…)`):\n95|\n96|```\n97|state=\"stale\"  winner={Epoch:1 LeaseID:aaaaaaaa-…}  warnings=[stale_process]\n98|```\n99|\n100|The host holding the strictly greater lease is reported stale with a\n101|`stale_process` warning — a wrong `SessionState` value under AC row 1 and a wrong\n102|winner story under AC row 2.\n103|\n104|**Mutant R1** — the candidate fix `Compare(...) >= 0` — **SURVIVED** both gates.\n105|The suite does not distinguish the two, so nothing pins the current behaviour\n106|either way. (Applying the candidate fix and seeing whether the suite notices is\n107|the check that separates \"intended\" from \"unmeasured\": it is unmeasured.)\n108|\n109|**F1 and F2 together refute the outcome's claim** \"26 applied, 26 killed, 0\n110|survivors. No surviving mutant exists, so no survival bound is owed.\" Both are\n111|narrowing mutants on production gates inside AC rows 2 and 3; the battery's\n112|12 narrowing rows touch `Compare`, the gap arm, the transition table, the retry\n113|gates, the provider arms, the lease-linkage arms and the parked branch, but not\n114|one of them reaches `resolveWinner`'s off-chain bookkeeping or `applyLocalLease`.\n115|The denominator excluded the half of the winner derivation that carries the\n116|defects.\n117|\n118|## F3 — the event census's denominator is one function name; a second handling\n119|## site with a wrong effect walks through everything\n120|\n121|`deriveHandledEventTypes` (census_state_test.go) inspects only\n122|`FuncDecl.Name == \"effect\"`. Plant **PA**: a new production file\n123|`internal/sessstate/zz_plant.go` declaring\n124|\n125|```go\n126|func (fold *chainFold) effectExtra(event Event, what string) error {\n127|    switch event.Type {\n128|    case \"session.reaped\":\n129|        return fold.step(StateIdle, what)\n130|    }\n131|    return nil\n132|}\n133|```\n134|\n135|wired into the production switch by the one-line, line-count-preserving edit\n136|`default: return nil` → `default: return fold.effectExtra(event, name)`.\n137|\n138|Result: **SURVIVED** — `behavioral=PASS full=PASS`. An unknown v1 event type now\n139|moves `running → idle`, directly contradicting the Section 5.2 inert rule this\n140|package claims to enforce and its own\n141|`TestReduceTreatsUnknownV1TypeAsInert` (which drives a different spelling,\n142|`session.future_probe`). All three censuses stay green: the refusal census sees\n143|no new `refuse` site, the state census sees no new spelling, and the event census\n144|never looks outside `