ns. Nothing in the producer's evidence shows the harness can\n184|report **SURVIVED** — the outcome that every one of the 26 KILLED rows is\n185|measured against — and `README.md` advertises them as \"plus NOT_APPLIED and\n186|COMPILE_FAIL controls\" without that distinction.\n187|\n188|I supplied the missing control: **R0**, behaviour-neutral and line-count\n189|preserving (`tailEventID` returning `\"\" + fold.tailID`) → **SURVIVED**. With\n190|R3–R10 (8 compiling known-bad mutants, all `behavioral=FAIL`) the instrument is\n191|sound in both directions — but that is my evidence, not the delivered evidence.\n192|Ship a real pair: one neutral mutant that must survive, one known-bad that must\n193|redden, both reaching the gates.\n194|\n195|## F6 (minor) — `scalar.ParseUUIDv7` is an unmeasured audit row and an\n196|## unsupported doc claim\n197|\n198|`doc.go:36-37` and `README.md:1775` name `scalar.ParseUUIDv7` among the watched\n199|owner delegations \"for digest and UUID grammars\". It has **zero** occurrences in\n200|`internal/sessstate` production (`environ.CheckUUIDv7` does that work). The\n201|alias-audit row can never fire, and the documentation states a delegation the\n202|package does not make.\n203|\n204|## F7 (minor) — an empty chain skips union validation entirely\n205|\n206|`Reduce` returns `creating` before `resolveWinner` when `len(input.Events) == 0`,\n207|so `Input.Union` and `Input.Local` are neither validated nor applied:\n208|\n209|```\n210|Union: [{4, \"not-a-uuid\"}, {}]  ->  state=\"creating\"  winner={0 \"\"}  err=<nil>\n211|```\n212|\n213|The same union on a non-empty chain refuses `ErrInvalidEvent` at\n214|`sessstate.go:920` / `:923`. Make it a gate or a stated bound in `doc.go`.\n215|\n216|---\n217|\n218|## Reviewer mutation battery (13 mutants; 10 killed, 3 survived)\n219|\n220|| ID | Mutation | Result |\n221|| --- | --- | --- |\n222|| R0 | neutral: `tailEventID` returns `\"\" + fold.tailID` | **SURVIVED** (negative control, as intended) |\n223|| R0b | `if found.Parked` → `if found == nil \\|\\| found.Parked` | SURVIVED — my error, the arm is unreachable (`found == nil` already returned); a second neutral control, not a positive one |\n224|| R1 | `Compare(local, Winner) == 0` → `>= 0` | **SURVIVED** — F2 |\n225|| R2 | delete the `case 0:` off-chain reset in `resolveWinner` | **SURVIVED** — F1 |\n226|| R3 | `staleSources` admits `stopped` | KILLED — `TestProjectLeavesStoppedPastTakeoverUnstaled` |\n227|| R4 | transition table admits `running → stopped` | KILLED — `TestReduceRefusesUnlistedTransitions/running-to-stopped` |\n228|| R5 | `noteCheckpoint` keeps the oldest instead of the newest | KILLED — `TestProjectDerivesFullLifecycle` |\n229|| R6 | provider version recorded even on record mismatch | KILLED — `TestProviderMismatchKeepsRecordPinned` |\n230|| R7 | local role inverted | KILLED — `TestProjectDerivesFullLifecycle`, `TestProjectIsIdempotentAcrossReads` |\n231|| R8 | `stale_process` warning suppressed | KILLED — `TestProjectDerivesLocalStale` |\n232|| R9 | epoch-gap conflict only past a jump of 3 | KILLED — `TestWinnerResolutionGap` |\n233|| R10 | losing-branch conflict dropped for epoch-1 rivals | KILLED — `TestWinnerResolutionTie`, `…TieOrdersBytewise`, `…PastEpochTie` |\n234|\n235|Every row above compiles and reaches both gates, so the denominator is 13 of 13\n236|applied; killed-over-applied is 10/13, with the three survivors named.\n237|\n238|---\n239|\n240|## Checked and clean (probed, refuted as findings — do not re-litigate)\n241|\n242|- **`task_board.launched.state` and `session.stopped.closure_kind` are not admit\n243|  holes.** Both `else` arms looked ungated on reading, but the canonical owner\n244|  closes them upstream: `core_records.go:859` `enum(\"state\",\"running\",\"idle\")`\n245|  and `core_records.go:742` `requireEnum(…,\"checkpointed\",\"bootstrap_abort\")`.\n246|  Fixtures carrying `\"tombstoned\"` / `\"crashed\"` are rejected by\n247|  `CalculateObjectIdentity` before the