74|---\n275|\n276|## What to do next\n277|\n278|1. Fix `resolveWinner`'s `case 0:` arm (F1) and `applyLocalLease`'s comparison\n279|   (F2), and pin each with a test that fails on the current code — a duplicated\n280|   off-chain union entry, and a local lease strictly greater than the winner.\n281|   Verify one step away from the finding vector, not only at it.\n282|2. Widen the event census denominator so a second production dispatch on\n283|   `event.Type` cannot be invisible (F3), and keep PA as a control plant.\n284|3. Re-derive and correct the 67/26 numbers in `README.md` and the outcome (F4).\n285|4. Add a real pair of harness controls that reach the gates — one neutral mutant\n286|   that must survive, one known-bad that must redden (F5).\n287|5. Fix or drop the `scalar.ParseUUIDv7` claim (F6) and gate-or-bound the\n288|   empty-chain union path (F7).\n289|6. Extend the battery's narrowing rows to the union/local-lease derivation; the\n290|   current denominator excludes it.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
