{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c615","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07db8-a28a-7e80-8be1-e3a988123386"},"sequence":357,"recorded_at":1780531400000709,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4385e4d6-e071-42f2-a438-a44213370546","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"4385e4d6-e071-42f2-a438-a44213370546","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4385e4d6-e071-42f2-a438-a44213370546"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"4278e1f9-e204-4af8-8e2c-68dde8830edb"},"task_id":"4278e1f9-e204-4af8-8e2c-68dde8830edb","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"4278e1f9-e204-4af8-8e2c-68dde8830edb","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(1754 line(s) above)\n1755|\n1756|Run the focused tests and coverage with:\n1757|\n1758|```bash\n1759|go test ./internal/sessstate -count=1\n1760|go test ./internal/sessstate -cover -count=1\n1761|```\n1762|\n1763|The unfiltered package run derives the 67-site refusal inventory from the\n1764|production source through `internal/invcore` (39 in `sessstate.go`, 26 in\n1765|`decode.go`, 2 in `project.go`): every `refuse` call site must have a\n1766|boundary-driven negative path (`Reduce`, `DecodeRecord`, `DecodeEvent`,\n1767|`Project`), every exercised site must derive, sentinel wraps outside the\n1768|funnel fail, and the observed sentinel set must equal the derived roster. A\n1769|second derived census covers the 11 `SessionState` spellings — structurally\n1770|derived from the `State`-typed const block, each living exactly once as a\n1771|production literal, each driven to through the production `Reduce` entry —\n1772|and a third covers the 24 handled v1 event types against the pinned Section\n1773|5.2 registry, each row naming its lifecycle-or-fact class and driver. The\n1774|alias audit keeps the funnel and the watched owner delegations\n1775|(`DecodeStrictObject`, `CheckUUIDv7`, `CheckUint53Bounds`, `ParseDigest`,\n1776|`ParseUUIDv4`, `ParseUUIDv7`, `ParseProviderID`, `ParseID`) in direct-call\n1777|position, proved by plants that include an import alias and a var binding in\n1778|both directions. The mutation battery (26 applied, 26 killed, 0 survivors; 12\n1779|narrowing, 8 arm-deletion, 3 census-test, 3 audit-only; plus NOT_APPLIED and\n1780|COMPILE_FAIL controls) covers the reduce, decode, and project paths —\n1781|including the tie, the gap, the parked channel, and the TestMain-only audit\n1782|layer — and is recorded on the owning task board item.\n1783|\n1784|## Structured Errors, Stable Codes, and Causal Redaction\n1785|\n1786|[`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror) implements the Section 15 Structured\n1787|Error contract: the closed versioned failure object, its stable code-to-exit\n1788|registry, its retryability rule, its typed diagnostic details, and the redaction\n1789|that keeps a local cause off the wire. The package holds no state, opens no\n1790|file, starts no process, and mutates nothing durable, so it has no crash or\n1791|idempotency surface and advertises no provider, platform, backend, or CLI\n1792|capability.\n1793|\n1794|| Element | Where it is decided |\n1795|| --- | --- |\n1796|| Versions `1.0.0`, `1.1.0`, `1.2.0`, `1.3.0` | `Version` constants; any other value, including major 2, is refused rather than coerced |\n1797|| Code-to-exit registry | `ExitCodeFor`, projected from the reviewed catalog rather than retyped, and admitting a code only for the versions that register it |\n1798|| Exit-status registry | `ExitStatusMeaning` and `IsFailureExitStatus`, the closed Section 15.2 table, whose eighteen rows are measured from [`internal/specdoc`](internal/specdoc) rather than restated in prose; success is never a failure class |\n1799|| Containing-contract binding | `BindingFor`, a static table with no negotiation path; `DecodeBound` takes the version from the container, never from the payload |\n1800|| Retryability | `RetryabilityRefusal`, quoting the clause that disqualifies each exit class and each individually named code |\n1801|| Typed details | `TargetAuth` and `RealmEvidence`, plus a presence requirement on `target_auth_missing` that the generic constructor cannot bypass |\n1802|| Redaction | `ValidateDetails` exact-key scanner over the four Section 15.1 detail classes, and `refuseCausalLeak` over the local cause chain |\n1803|| Detail ownership | `New` deep-copies the caller's diagnostic graph and `Detail` deep-copies on the way out, so the graph `ValidateDetails` checked is the graph the object encodes |\n1804|| Untrusted boundaries | `LocalFromUntrusted`, which takes no part of a child or peer payload |\n1805|\n1806|The exit status is never a constructor argument. `New` takes a `Spec` with no\n1807|`exit_code` field and resolves the status through `ExitCodeFor`, so a call site\n1808|cannot mint a mapping the specification does not assign. The reader is the\n1809|mirror image: a code the registry does not carry is admitted, because Section\n1810|15.3 permits a code added in a compatible minor, but it keeps its envelope's\n1811|exit class, is reported by `CodeRegistered` as unrecognized, and can never carry\n1812|the success status.\n1813|\n1814|Redaction is two decidable gates and one structural property, and none of them\n(more lines below)"}}}
