ns. The mutation battery (26 applied, 26 killed, 0 survivors; 12\n1779|narrowing, 8 arm-deletion, 3 census-test, 3 audit-only; plus NOT_APPLIED and\n1780|COMPILE_FAIL controls) covers the reduce, decode, and project paths —\n1781|including the tie, the gap, the parked channel, and the TestMain-only audit\n1782|layer — and is recorded on the owning task board item.\n1783|\n1784|## Structured Errors, Stable Codes, and Causal Redaction\n1785|\n1786|[`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror) implements the Section 15 Structured\n1787|Error contract: the closed versioned failure object, its stable code-to-exit\n1788|registry, its retryability rule, its typed diagnostic details, and the redaction\n1789|that keeps a local cause off the wire. The package holds no state, opens no\n1790|file, starts no process, and mutates nothing durable, so it has no crash or\n1791|idempotency surface and advertises no provider, platform, backend, or CLI\n1792|capability.\n1793|\n1794|| Element | Where it is decided |\n1795|| --- | --- |\n1796|| Versions `1.0.0`, `1.1.0`, `1.2.0`, `1.3.0` | `Version` constants; any other value, including major 2, is refused rather than coerced |\n1797|| Code-to-exit registry | `ExitCodeFor`, projected from the reviewed catalog rather than retyped, and admitting a code only for the versions that register it |\n1798|| Exit-status registry | `ExitStatusMeaning` and `IsFailureExitStatus`, the closed Section 15.2 table, whose eighteen rows are measured from [`internal/specdoc`](internal/specdoc) rather than restated in prose; success is never a failure class |\n1799|| Containing-contract binding | `BindingFor`, a static table with no negotiation path; `DecodeBound` takes the version from the container, never from the payload |\n1800|| Retryability | `RetryabilityRefusal`, quoting the clause that disqualifies each exit class and each individually named code |\n1801|| Typed details | `TargetAuth` and `RealmEvidence`, plus a presence requirement on `target_auth_missing` that the generic constructor cannot bypass |\n1802|| Redaction | `ValidateDetails` exact-key scanner over the four Section 15.1 detail classes, and `refuseCausalLeak` over the local cause chain |\n1803|| Detail ownership | `New` deep-copies the caller's diagnostic graph and `Detail` deep-copies on the way out, so the graph `ValidateDetails` checked is the graph the object encodes |\n1804|| Untrusted boundaries | `LocalFromUntrusted`, which takes no part of a child or peer payload |\n1805|\n1806|The exit status is never a constructor argument. `New` takes a `Spec` with no\n1807|`exit_code` field and resolves the status through `ExitCodeFor`, so a call site\n1808|cannot mint a mapping the specification does not assign. The reader is the\n1809|mirror image: a code the registry does not carry is admitted, because Section\n1810|15.3 permits a code added in a compatible minor, but it keeps its envelope's\n1811|exit class, is reported by `CodeRegistered` as unrecognized, and can never carry\n1812|the success status.\n1813|\n1814|Redaction is two decidable gates and one structural property, and none of them\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c61b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07db8-a28a-7e80-8be1-e3a988123386"},"sequence":360,"recorded_at":1780531400000715,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"4385e4d6-e071-42f2-a438-a44213370546","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"4385e4d6-e071-42f2-a438-a44213370546","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"4385e4d6-e071-42f2-a438-a44213370546"},"call_id":"call_01a07db9ee7f7973bbea4075950b9680","text":"Read text file `internal/sessstate/project.go`.\n1|package sessstate\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessrepo\"\n5|)\n6|\n7|// Projector binds the pure reducer to one repository. It only reads:\n8|// ListSessions locates the session (and its parked channel), GetRecord\n9|// and ListEvents with GetEvent load the authoritative bytes, and\n10|// Decode plus Reduce derive the projection. No entry here mutates\n11|// durable state, so there is no crash window to arm: placing\n12|// secconftest points around reads would measure nothing, and a crashed\n13|// read retries as the same read. Idempotency is the reducer's purity —\n14|// projecting twice yields the identical projection — pinned by\n15|// TestProjectIsIdempotentAcrossReads.\n16|type Projector struct {\n17|\t// Repo is the session repository to project from. It is required.\n18|\tRepo *sessrepo.Repository\n19|\t// LocalHostID selects the local role: the owner host of the\n20|\t// newest authoritative event decides owner against replica. Empty\n21|\t// leaves the role unknown rather than guessing.\n22|\tLocalHostID string\n23|\t// Union carries competing off-chain leases observed at mesh union\n24|\t// for winner resolution. Nil projects the chain alone.\n25|\tUnion []LeaseHead\n26|\t// Local is the lease the local host acts under for the stale\n27|\t// projection. Zero disables the stale override.\n28|\tLocal LeaseHead\n29|}\n30|\n31|// Project derives the session projection for one session ID. A parked\n32|// session returns the parked state with its blocking reason and retry,\n33|// never an error or an omission; an ID with no listing entry refuses\n34|// unknown. The listing therefore tells a parked name apart from a\n35|// missing one with no sessrepo interface change.\n36|func (projector *Projector) Project(sessionID string) (Projection, error) {\n37|\tif projector == nil || projector.Repo == nil {\n38|\t\treturn Projection{}, refuse(ErrDerivation, \"projector carries no repository\")\n39|\t}\n40|\tsummaries, err := projector.Repo.ListSessions()\n41|\tif err != nil {\n42|\t\treturn Projection{}, err\n43|\t}\n44|\tvar found *sessrepo.SessionSummary\n45|\tfor index := range summaries {\n46|\t\tif summaries[index].SessionID == sessionID {\n47|\t\t\tfound = &summaries[index]\n48|\t\t\tbreak\n49|\t\t}\n50|\t}\n51|\tif found == nil {\n52|\t\treturn Projection{}, refuse(ErrUnknownSession, \"no session %s\", sessionID)\n53|\t}\n54|\tif found.Parked {\n55|\t\treturn Reduce(Input{\n56|\t\t\tRecord: Record{\n57|\t\t\t\tSessionID:  found.SessionID,\n58|\t\t\t\tRecordID:   found.RecordID,\n59|\t\t\t\tName:       found.Name,\n60|\t\t\t\tKind:       found.Kind,\n61|\t\t\t\tProviderID: found.ProviderID,\n62|\t\t\t},\n63|\t\t\tParked: &ParkedFacts{\n64|\t\t\t\tBlockingReason: found.BlockingReason,\n65|\t\t\t\tRetryHint:      found.RetryHint,\n66|\t\t\t},\n67|\t\t})\n68|\t}\n69|\trecordBytes, err := projector.Repo.GetRecord(sessionID)\n70|\tif err != nil {\n71|\t\treturn Projection{}, err\n72|\t}\n73|\trecord, err := DecodeRecord(recordBytes)\n74|\tif err != nil {\n75|\t\treturn Projection{}, err\n76|\t}\n77|\tindexed, err := projector.Repo.ListEvents(sessionID)\n78|\tif err != nil {\n79|\t\treturn Projection{}, err\n80|\t}\n81|\tevents := make([]Event, 0, len(indexed))\n82|\tfor _, summary := range indexed {\n83|\t\tblob, err := projector.Repo.GetEvent(sessionID, summary.EventID)\n84|\t\tif err != nil {\n85|\t\t\treturn Projection{}, err\n86|\t\t}\n87|\t\tevent, err := DecodeEvent(blob)\n88|\t\tif err != nil {\n89|\t\t\treturn Projection{}, err\n90|\t\t}\n91|\t\tevents = append(events, event)\n92|\t}\n93|\treturn Reduce(Input{\n94|\t\tRecord:      record,\n95|\t\tEvents:      events,\n96|\t\tUnion:       append([]LeaseHead(nil), projector.Union...),\n97|\t\tLocal:       projector.Local,\n98|\t\tLocalHostID: projector.LocalHostID,\n99|\t})\n100|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
