ant → exit 1 `sessrepo content-equality site without a registered vector: plantextra.go:6`; P3 `string(left) == string(right)` plant in `store.go` → exit 1 `...: store.go:17`. The three plant tests that diffed synthetic sources against hard-coded ledger copies are now coupled to the live derived set and live ledger, so drift fails the sanity half first.\\n- NUMBERS (re-derived, not re-typed): refusal census 35 = chain.go 25 + sessrepo.go 5 + store.go 5 (README's 36 fixed in place); equality census 2 sites = 2 ledger rows; battery 33 applied / 33 killed / 0 survivors (16 narrowing N1–N16, 10 arm-deletion D1–D10, 4 census-only C1–C4 incl. both reviewer plant shapes, 3 audit-only A1–A3) + NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL controls distinct. Candidate tree by detached-index `write-tree`; outcome enumerates exactly the 11 CR paths. Also fixed the N2 comment wording (`sessrepo_test.go`): the canonical owner refuses one arm later, not earlier (member arms run before Verify).\\n- GATES this session: `go build` 0, `go vet` 0, `GOOS=windows` vet+build 0, gofmt clean, `go test ./...` 0 (24/24), `-race` 0 in 4 groups (24 unique pkgs), tracecheck 0 (60/98), sessrepo cover 87.6%.\\n- STATUS: handed off to review (rev4).\\n\\n### wbpf1v round 2: F1/F2/F3 rework — resume heals every create window, load arms witnessed, allowlist anchored\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-wbpf1v rework after rev1 `changes_requested` (F1 false ordering claim, F2 five surviving load/recovery mutants, F3 interrupted-create brick; F4 non-blocking allowlist anchoring fixed while here). Same worktree/branch, still uncommitted for the board CR.\\n- F1 CORRECTION (supersedes the round-1 entry below): \\\"schema gate precedes every Verify call\\\" was false — `loadSessionLocked` re-verifies stored blobs through Verify with no schema gate, and the verbatim SPEC §5.5 provider-identity record verifies cleanly there (recomputed digest matches; only `field != SelfEventID` refuses). Restated everywhere the false universal stood (`identity.go` comment, `identity_test.go` bound, `sessrepo/doc.go` authority split, README, outcome): entry decodes gate schema before Verify; the load path recomputes whatever digest stored bytes claim and refuses non-`event_id` self fields / index-disagreeing digests at named arms. Gating the load path instead would have made the field arm unreachable-by-construction (Verify resolves the self field from the same schema member) and its narrowing mutant unkillable — measured, not assumed. The load verify is now three single-line refuse rows (verify failure, self field, digest), each with its own boundary plant; the shared message that formatted a nil error is gone.\\n- F3 FIX: `CreateSession` (MkdirAll dir → record → MkdirAll events → chain) had both crash points outside its span, and a crash before `record.json` was unrecoverable (`ErrSessionExists` for a never-created session; `GetRecord`/`ListSessions` corrupt, the latter for the whole repo). `resumeCreateLocked` now heals both parked states (bare directory completes with the retry bytes when no chain exists; record-without-chain completes as before; chain-without-record and colliding bytes refuse), and `AfterCreateStep` fires after each of the four steps so one secconftest point per boundary drives it — each test asserts the exact fired-step prefix plus arm consumption. Interior faults carry `recoverable_parked_state` (parked state the identical retry resumes); `safe_retry` stays pre-span only.\\n- F2 BATTERY: 26 applied / 26 killed / 0 survivors (12 narrowing, 10 arm-deletion, 2 census-only, 2 audit-only; NOT_APPLIED + COMPILE_FAIL distinct), denominator extended to load/recovery: provider-identity plant kills the field narrowing (M1a), blob-swap kills the digest narrowing (M1b), exclusive-create-first blob install kills O_EXCL→O_TRUNC (M2, witnessed through a fresh handle sharing no mutex/memory), same-length collision kills the resume-equality narrowing (M6), cross-session record kills the session-half drop (M7), rebound-predecessor detached index kills the digest-half drop behaviorally (M8 — the old detached test passes via the continuity arm and is kept as the precision control). Measured bound: the verify-error arm is behaviorally subsumed by the field arm (Verify returns field \\\"\\\" on every error path) — diagnostic attribution + census row, no deletion mutant, stated in the outcome. Harness at `.temp/TASK-260830-wbpf1v/mutation_battery.sh` (gitignored scratch) with exact-count application and checksum restore; log attached to the board task.\\n- F4 FIX: allowlist anchored on `<root>/internal/sessrepo/` with the site count pinned at exactly 3 (decode ×2 + load ×1); a synthetic-tree test plants `internal/provhost/sessrepo/` (token preserved, owner changed) and `internal/xsessrepo/` and requires both outside, leaf inside.\\n- F5 NOTE (verdict non-blocking, out of the spawn brief — acknowledged, not rewired): `syncDirectory`/`writeAtomic`/`writeExclusive`/`installEventBlob` duplicate `localstore` path policy (which has no consumer yet); the outcome's \\\"no new path policy\\\" line is corrected to state the duplication with the reason instead of claiming otherwise.\\n- GATES: full `go test ./...`, `-race` over all packages, `-cover`, `go vet` + `GOOS=windows` vet/build, gofmt, tracecheck, catalog freshness, cigate selections — all re-run this session (see outcome for exit codes).\\n- STATUS: handed off to review (rev2).\\n\\n### wbpf1v: session repository + event chain landed; provhost attestation bound rewritten around the new truth\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260830-wbpf1v (first leaf of STORY-260830-3tq4ns, root of M1 chain). New `internal/sessrepo` (doc/sessrepo/chain/store + behavioral/crash/census tests), README section, `internal/provhost/identity.go` comment + `identity_test.go` gate rewrite. Work left uncommitted in the story worktree for the board CR.\\n- FINDING (gate did its job): `go test ./...` reddened on `TestNoProductionPathAttestsProviderIdentityBinding`, which pins \\\"no production file calls VerifyObjectIdentity\\\". Session-record/event persistence MUST attest (SPEC §5.1/§5.2 \\\"MUST recompute and MUST reject\\\"); routing through `CalculateObjectIdentity` would dodge the text scan while attesting anyway, so the bound was rewritten, not bypassed: `internal/sessrepo/` allowlisted (schema gate precedes every Verify call, so provider-identity records can never reach one), every other tree still red (proved by a temporary foreign call site, then removed), exception fails when stale. Reviewers read the provhost diff first.\\n- DELIVERY: CreateSession/AppendEvent over content-addressed no-replace blobs + atomic chain index; gap/repeat/divergent/stale/predecessor arms; first-event record link; byte-identical reload across handles; idempotent retry; secconftest prepare/commit faults (safe_retry / recoverable_parked_state, crashed commit counts as committed); local Resolve (exact, ASCII-fold ambiguity, UUID route); 34-site invcore census all boundary-driven with alias/var/dot-import/shadow plants.\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-wbpf1v_outcome.md` on the board task (10/10 AC rows with call sites, gate table, census + 12/12 killed mutation battery with narrowing/arm-deletion/census-only/audit-only + NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL rows, tree OID + exact changed paths recorded there). Battery harness at `/tmp/mutation_battery.sh` (throwaway, not committed).\\n- GATES: `go test ./...` exit 0 (24 ok), `-race` exit 0 (all 24 pkgs, 4 groups), `-cover` (sessrepo 86.3/provhost 86.0), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows` vet/build exit 0, gofmt clean, tracecheck exit 0, catalog current, cigate contract + claims selections exit 0, fuzz count 13 (smoke not run: no fuzzed package touched).\\n- STATUS: handed off to review. Downstream bounds in outcome: single-branch chain, no reducer/name-resolution/CLI/lease-arbitration in this leaf.\\n\\n### 9ny4xl: R1–R6 closed — probe-availability claims corrected, marker census measures effect, catalog directive pinned\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260907-9ny4xl (story final leaf). `internal/cigate` claim tests + effect census + splitter tests + `doc.go`, `internal/catalog` directive pin, `.github/workflows/ci.yml` comments + freshness guard, README CI table + 20 probe notes, 2249 correction below. Leaves 1–5 production untouched; `claims.go` production changed only in comments; `catalog.go` production unchanged.\\n- R1: the capability-claims comment and the 2249 entry stated `ProbeState.Available` is consumed by no call site; `claims.go:235` reads it into the availability map. Both now state what `doc.go` states: the gate reads `Available` from its input states (both postures driven), and what reaches no availability reader is the live probe outcome (`ProbeStates` feeds only `CapabilityIDs`, which drops availability). New `TestAvailabilityFieldDrivesVerdict` refuses/admits the same claim across postures (battery N-avail-false/true killed).\\n- R2: the derive-targets comment named the grep + size check as the fail-closed guards. Re-measured with a real empty-leg replica (`secconftest` + fuzzless `axerror`): grep refuses nothing (pipeline status discarded), `test -s` passes (8 lines), only the count pin refuses (8 vs 13, exit 1). Comment now names the pin; neighbouring steps audited (PASS-guard loops, gofmt/coverage/fixture count guards, target-match diff, elapsed grep) — no same mistake.\\n- R3: the marker census measured occurrence while markers classified 0 of 2 mentions. New `TestEveryNonClaimMarkerClassifiesCorpusSentence` asserts the resolving arm per mention from the production predicates cross-checked against the production verdict, and requires every marker to sole-classify at least one corpus sentence. 20 probe notes added to the README CI section (one sole-classifier per marker); measured distribution negation 2 / marker 20 / refused 0. README cell corrected to \\\"negated or marker-classified non-claim context\\\". Old corpus + new census fails (battery C-old-corpus); dropped-list X3 now dies (was a survivor).\\n- R4: new `TestSameBlockSentencesSplitOnTerminal` (period/bang/query rows, same-block negated+positive pair) kills the paragraph-granularity narrowing (N-split-X1) and the dot-only narrowing (N-split-dot-only).\\n- R5 (bound, re-measured this session): 13/13 smoke targets print `fuzz: elapsed`; `secconftest/FuzzRedactCorpus` + all four `canonicaljson` targets spend `-fuzztime=100x` on baseline coverage and never print `now fuzzing` (8 reach mutation). Stated in the README row and the smoke-step comment with the escape (budget/corpus change moves it silently).\\n- R6 (bound ANSWERED): the rev2 \\\"Linux execution unverified\\\" unknown is closed by the landing PR run — PR #36 (STORY-260830-1i3qu7, merged 2026-09-06) shows `Conformance fixtures (ubuntu-latest, internal/secprim)` and `(ubuntu-latest, internal/secconftest)` pass in both runs, with macOS legs and every other job green (`gh pr checks 36`, observed this session).\\n- CARRIED (pre-existing, fixed here): `//go:generate` → `// go:generate` disarmed the generator while the token survived and the freshness diff stayed clean (reproduced: old step exits 0 on the rewrite). Fix: anchored `grep -c '^//go:generate'` pin in the freshness step + committed `TestGenerateDirectiveStaysRecognizedForm`; the rewrite now fails the guard (exit 1) and the pin while catalog/cataloggen stay otherwise green (battery G-directive-space, behavioral suite executed).\\n- RECORDED (pre-existing, not fixed — traceability scope): `TestCIWorkflowInvokesTraceabilityGate` is a `bytes.Contains` gate over `ci.yml`: moving the Vet step's `run: go vet ./...` into a YAML comment keeps it green (doubly blind — `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` carries the same substring). Re-attacked this session (PASS on the blinded tree, ci.yml restored byte-identical). At HEAD before every leaf of both stories; named here beside the `go:generate` one per the rev2 verdict.\\n- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260907-9ny4xl_outcome.md` (5/5 AC rows with call sites, battery table, tree OID, exact changed paths) + `TASK-260907-9ny4xl_mutants.log` + `TASK-260907-9ny4xl_change-request.patch` on the board task. Battery 14 applied / 14 killed / 0 survivors (narrowing 10 incl. the token-preserving directive rewrite, arm-deletion 3, census-only 1; C-old-corpus census control; NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL distinct harness rows; audit-only 0 — no AST audit in this CR's scope).\\n- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (23 ok), `-race ./...` exit 0 (23 ok, full repo), `-cover` exit 0 (cigate 90.5%, secprim 94.4%, secconftest 92.6%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` exit 0 (60 contracts / 98 cases, unchanged), catalog current, capability-claims + contract-preservation steps verbatim 6/6 + 6/6, fuzz smoke 13/13 elapsed (5 baseline-only, 8 mutation).\\n- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps). Story-final CR: no board element created under STORY-260905-3t31e9; follow-up needs are listed in the outcome, not the board.\\n\\n### 33xcnc round 2: review F1/F2/F3 closed test-only, 70/71 battery on the corrected 101-exit denominator\\n- SCOPE (test-only; no production touched, frozen files intact): `internal/environ/shape_census_test.go` (load-bearing delegation pins + 9 synthetic decoy controls), `tuple_agreement_test.go` (uppercase-hex fingerprint vector), `frame_agreement_test.go` (per-member duplicate sweeper over 30 production-derived keys × 4 judges), `decode_unit_test.go` (R_digestnonstr downstream pin), `internal/provhost/protocol_test.go` (DecodeResponse per-member duplicate test, 6 derived + 4 foreign keys).\\n- F1 (decoy defeated the gate): `pinsCheckDelegation`/`pinsDelegation` required only an `environ` reference, so `_, _ = environ.CheckDigest(raw)` + a regrown `ParseDigest(ToLower)` copy stayed green while `sessadapter.DecodeTuple` admitted uppercase-hex fingerprints `environ` refuses. Fix: helpers must be exactly `return environ.Twin(args)` with twin-name match; wrappers must attribute the owner verdict to reused non-blank names with no other call, plus a duplicate-rule check. The plant now fails `TestCheckHelpersDelegateToEnviron` AND `TestTupleAgreementAcrossFacades/uppercase_fingerprint_refused`; harness mutants D1/D2 report `suites=behavioral,census`.\\n- F2 (duplicate class measured at one key): narrowing `duplicate && key != K` survived 6/8 response keys and 7/10 owner keys. Fix: derivation-backed sweepers (member sets derived from tuple/observation/response/scan-request production; new members auto-swept) through `DecodeTuple`/`CheckScanRequest`/`DecodeManifest`/`DecodeResponse`/`DecodeStrictObject`. Battery adds 8 owner + 6 retained narrowing mutants, one per survived key. Survivor honest-report: first `P_dupnarrow_provider_id` run SURVIVED and exposed a real test gap (foreign `provider_id` missing from the envelope sweeper); key added, mutant re-run KILLED.\\n- F3 (denominator basis): corrected — 31 refuse sites + 59 bool-false + 11 `&Fault{}` frame exits = 101 (105 counting the 4 bool-`return <expr>` arms: CheckEnvironmentID/CheckSemver/isNull/rawUint53-forward). The \\\"27 of 100\\\" figure was the corrected basis pre-ladder-guard; 90 was the uncorrected one. Harness derives all three components at runtime; F3 residue exits attacked by N1/M15/M15n/M16/M17/M17n inside the previously excluded 11.\\n- EVIDENCE: battery `/tmp/mutbattery_leaf6/run.py` + `battery.log` + `results.json`: 70 killed / 71 applied (49 narrowing incl. D1 token-preserving delegation decoy + 8 owner + 6 retained duplicate narrowings; 17 arm-deletion incl. D2; 3 census-only; 1 audit-only; H1 NOT_APPLIED + H2 COMPILE_FAIL distinct rows; 1 predicted survivor R_digestnonstr, now property-pinned by `TestDigestBridgeRefusesEmptyDownstream`). Mutant table + outcome attached as round-2 resources.\\n...\\n8:### TASK-260830-1r9wrr: session-state reducer landed; no re-attestation outside the leaf\\n12:- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-1r9wrr_outcome.md` on the board task (10/10 AC rows with call sites, gate table, three censuses, 26/26 killed battery with narrowing/arm-deletion/census-test/audit-only + NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL rows, tree OID + exact changed paths). Harness `.temp/TASK-260830-1r9wrr/mutate.sh` (gitignored scratch), log attached.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 19402,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 4851,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
